**18_sched** — tests weighted interval scheduling on half-open `[start, end)` intervals with a three-level tie-break (max total weight → fewest jobs → lexicographically smallest sorted id list); edge cases include zero-length jobs (always taken iff weight > 0, conflict with nothing), touching intervals, non-positive weights never selected, and string-order id sorting (`"j10" < "j2"`). The hidden grader runs fixed edge cases plus three seeded randomised phases (~560 cases) differentially against an exhaustive brute-force over all subsets implemented inside `test.py`, and also checks the input list is not mutated.
